@startuml authentication-flow
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 200

title User Authentication Flow - Expanded

actor User
participant "API\nController" as API
participant "MediatR pipeline\n(ValidationBehavior)" as Mediator
box "Handler Layer" #LightBlue
participant "RegisterUserHandler" as RegHandler
participant "LoginHandler" as LoginHandler
participant "RefreshTokenHandler" as RefreshHandler
participant "ConfirmUserHandler" as ConfirmHandler
participant "ResendConfirmationEmailHandler" as ResendHandler
participant "UpdateUsernameHandler" as UpdateUsernameHandler
participant "UpdateEmailHandler" as UpdateEmailHandler
participant "UpdatePasswordHandler" as UpdatePasswordHandler
participant "UpdateProfileHandler" as UpdateProfileHandler
participant "DeleteAccountHandler" as DeleteAccountHandler
participant "UserManager<ApplicationUser>" as UserMgr
participant "TokenService" as TokenSvc
end box
box "Infrastructure Layer" #LightGreen
participant "Argon2PasswordHasher" as Argon2
participant "JWT\nInfrastructure" as JWT
participant "Email\nProvider" as SMTP
participant "Template\nProvider" as Template
end box
box "Repository / Cross-slice" #LightYellow
participant "DapperUserStore\n(IUserStore/IUserPasswordStore/\nIUserEmailStore)" as UserStore
participant "EmailDispatcher\n(Features.Emails)" as EmailDispatcher
end box
database "SQL Server" as DB

note over UserMgr
  ASP.NET Core Identity's UserManager<TUser>
  replaces the deleted AuthRepository: handlers
  no longer issue SQL or call Argon2 directly,
  they delegate to UserManager, which in turn
  calls DapperUserStore (persistence) and
  Argon2PasswordHasher (IPasswordHasher<TUser>).
end note

== Registration Flow ==

User -> API: POST /api/auth/register\n{username, firstName, lastName,\nemail, dateOfBirth, password}
activate API

API -> Mediator: Send(RegisterUserCommand)
activate Mediator

note right of Mediator
  ValidationBehavior runs RegisterUserValidator
  (FluentValidation) before the handler:
  - Username: 3-64 chars, alphanumeric + [._-]
  - Email: valid format, max 128 chars
  - Password: min 8 chars, uppercase,\n    lowercase, number, special char
  - DateOfBirth: must be 19+ years old
end note

alt Validation fails
  Mediator -> API: throws FluentValidation.ValidationException
  API -> User: 400 Bad Request\n{message: "Validation failed", errors: {...}}
else Validation succeeds
  Mediator -> RegHandler: Handle(command)
  activate RegHandler

  RegHandler -> RegHandler: user = new UserAccount{...}\n.ToApplicationUser()

  RegHandler -> UserMgr: CreateAsync(user, password)
  activate UserMgr

  UserMgr -> Argon2: HashPassword(user, password)
  activate Argon2
  note right of Argon2
    Delegates to IPasswordInfrastructure.Hash:
    Argon2id parameters:
    - Salt: 16 bytes (128-bit)
    - Memory: 64MB
    - Iterations: 4
    - Parallelism: CPU count
    - Hash output: 32 bytes
  end note
  Argon2 --> UserMgr: "base64(salt):base64(hash)"
  deactivate Argon2

  UserMgr -> UserStore: SetPasswordHashAsync(user, hash)
  note right of UserStore
    user.Id is still empty at this point -
    only sets the in-memory hash. CreateAsync
    writes it to dbo.UserCredential itself.
  end note

  UserMgr -> UserStore: FindByNameAsync(username)
  activate UserStore
  UserStore -> DB: SELECT UserAccountID, Username, ...\nFROM dbo.UserAccount\nWHERE Username = @Username
  activate DB
  DB --> UserStore: null (user doesn't exist)
  deactivate DB
  deactivate UserStore

  UserMgr -> UserStore: FindByEmailAsync(email)
  activate UserStore
  UserStore -> DB: SELECT UserAccountID, Username, ...\nFROM dbo.UserAccount\nWHERE Email = @Email
  activate DB
  DB --> UserStore: null (email doesn't exist)
  deactivate DB
  deactivate UserStore
  note right of UserMgr
    Default UserManager validators check
    uniqueness before CreateAsync is called;
    DapperUserStore.CreateAsync also guards
    against a genuine race via a caught
    duplicate-key SqlException (2601/2627).
  end note

  UserMgr -> UserStore: CreateAsync(user)
  activate UserStore

  UserStore -> DB: BEGIN TRANSACTION
  activate DB
  UserStore -> DB: INSERT INTO dbo.UserAccount\n(Username, FirstName, LastName,\nDateOfBirth, Email)\nOUTPUT INSERTED.UserAccountID
  DB --> UserStore: UserAccountId (GUID)
  UserStore -> DB: INSERT INTO dbo.UserCredential\n(UserAccountId, Hash)
  UserStore -> DB: COMMIT TRANSACTION
  deactivate DB
  note right of UserStore
    Both statements run via Dapper's
    ExecuteScalarAsync/ExecuteAsync against
    a single DbTransaction, not a stored
    procedure - no manual parameter binding
  end note

  UserStore --> UserMgr: IdentityResult.Success\n(user.Id set)
  deactivate UserStore

  UserMgr --> RegHandler: IdentityResult
  deactivate UserMgr

  alt !result.Succeeded
    RegHandler -> Mediator: throw ConflictException\n(DuplicateUserName/DuplicateEmail codes ->\n"Username or email already exists";\notherwise joined error descriptions)
    Mediator -> API: propagate
    API -> User: 409 Conflict\n"Username or email already exists"
  else result.Succeeded

    RegHandler -> TokenSvc: GenerateAccessToken(user)
    activate TokenSvc
    TokenSvc -> JWT: GenerateJwt(userId, username, expiry)
    activate JWT
    note right of JWT
      JWT Configuration:
      - Algorithm: HS256
      - Expires: 1 hour
      - Claims:
        * sub: userId
        * unique_name: username
        * iat / jti
    end note
    JWT -> JWT: Create JWT with claims
    JWT -> JWT: Sign with secret key
    JWT --> TokenSvc: Access Token
    deactivate JWT
    TokenSvc --> RegHandler: Access Token
    deactivate TokenSvc

    RegHandler -> TokenSvc: GenerateRefreshToken(user)
    activate TokenSvc
    TokenSvc -> JWT: GenerateJwt(userId, username, expiry)
    activate JWT
    note right of JWT
      Refresh Token:
      - Expires: 21 days (504 hours)
      - Same structure as access token,\n    signed with a separate secret
    end note
    JWT --> TokenSvc: Refresh Token
    deactivate JWT
    TokenSvc --> RegHandler: Refresh Token
    deactivate TokenSvc

    RegHandler -> TokenSvc: GenerateConfirmationToken(user)
    activate TokenSvc
    TokenSvc -> JWT: GenerateJwt(userId, username, expiry)
    activate JWT
    note right of JWT
      Confirmation Token:
      - Expires: 30 minutes (0.5 hours)
      - Signed with a third, separate secret
    end note
    JWT --> TokenSvc: Confirmation Token
    deactivate JWT
    TokenSvc --> RegHandler: Confirmation Token
    deactivate TokenSvc

    RegHandler -> Mediator: Send(SendRegistrationEmailCommand)\n(Shared.Application cross-slice contract)
    activate Mediator
    Mediator -> EmailDispatcher: SendRegistrationEmailAsync(\n  firstName, email, confirmationToken)
    note right of Mediator
      Routed to Features.Emails'
      SendRegistrationEmailHandler,
      the only cross-slice call in
      the backend
    end note
    activate EmailDispatcher

    EmailDispatcher -> Template: RenderUserRegisteredEmailAsync(\n  firstName, confirmationLink)
    activate Template
    note right of Template
      Razor Component:
      - Header with branding
      - Welcome message
      - Confirmation button
      - Footer
    end note
    Template -> Template: Render Razor component\nto HTML
    Template --> EmailDispatcher: HTML email content
    deactivate Template

    EmailDispatcher -> SMTP: SendAsync(email, subject, body)
    activate SMTP
    note right of SMTP
      SMTP Configuration (MailKit):
      - Host/port: from env (SMTP_HOST/SMTP_PORT)
      - TLS: StartTLS when SMTP_USE_SSL=true
      - Auth: username/password, if configured
    end note
    SMTP -> SMTP: Build MIME message
    SMTP -> SMTP: Connect, authenticate,\nsend, disconnect
    SMTP --> EmailDispatcher: Success / throws
    deactivate SMTP

    deactivate EmailDispatcher
    deactivate Mediator

    alt Email sent successfully
      RegHandler -> RegHandler: emailSent = true
    else mediator.Send throws
      RegHandler -> RegHandler: catch(Exception),\nlog to stderr,\nemailSent = false
    end

    RegHandler --> Mediator: RegistrationPayload(\n  userAccountId, username,\n  refreshToken, accessToken,\n  confirmationEmailSent)
    deactivate RegHandler
    Mediator --> API: RegistrationPayload
    deactivate Mediator

    API -> User: 201 Created\n{\n  message: "User registered successfully.",\n  payload: {\n    userAccountId, username,\n    refreshToken, accessToken,\n    confirmationEmailSent\n  }\n}
  end
end
deactivate API

== Login Flow ==

User -> API: POST /api/auth/login\n{username, password}
activate API

API -> Mediator: Send(LoginCommand)
activate Mediator

note right of Mediator
  ValidationBehavior runs LoginValidator:
  username and password must both be non-empty
end note

alt Validation fails
  Mediator -> API: throws FluentValidation.ValidationException
  API -> User: 400 Bad Request\n{message: "Validation failed", errors: {...}}
else Validation succeeds

  Mediator -> LoginHandler: Handle(command)
  activate LoginHandler

  LoginHandler -> UserMgr: FindByNameAsync(username)
  activate UserMgr
  UserMgr -> UserStore: FindByNameAsync(username)
  activate UserStore
  UserStore -> DB: SELECT UserAccountID, Username, ...\nFROM dbo.UserAccount\nWHERE Username = @Username
  activate DB
  DB --> UserStore: UserAccount row or null
  deactivate DB
  UserStore -> UserStore: HydrateAsync\n(load active UserCredential.Hash,\nUserVerification -> EmailConfirmed)
  UserStore --> UserMgr: ApplicationUser or null
  deactivate UserStore
  UserMgr --> LoginHandler: ApplicationUser or null
  deactivate UserMgr

  alt User not found
    LoginHandler -> Mediator: throw UnauthorizedException\n"Invalid username or password."
    Mediator -> API: propagate
    API -> User: 401 Unauthorized
  else User found

    LoginHandler -> UserMgr: CheckPasswordAsync(user, password)
    activate UserMgr
    note right of UserMgr
      HasPasswordAsync short-circuits to false
      (no active UserCredential was hydrated)
      without calling the hasher; otherwise
      delegates to Argon2PasswordHasher.
    end note
    UserMgr -> Argon2: VerifyHashedPassword(\n  user, user.PasswordHash, password)
    activate Argon2
    note right of Argon2
      Delegates to IPasswordInfrastructure.Verify:
      1. Split stored hash: "salt:hash"
      2. Hash provided password with the same salt
      3. Constant-time comparison\n   (CryptographicOperations.FixedTimeEquals)
    end note
    Argon2 --> UserMgr: Success/Failed
    deactivate Argon2
    UserMgr --> LoginHandler: true/false
    deactivate UserMgr

    alt Password invalid
      LoginHandler -> Mediator: throw UnauthorizedException
      Mediator -> API: propagate
      API -> User: 401 Unauthorized
    else Password valid

      LoginHandler -> TokenSvc: GenerateAccessToken(user)
        activate TokenSvc
        TokenSvc -> JWT: GenerateJwt(...)
        activate JWT
        JWT --> TokenSvc: Access Token
        deactivate JWT
        TokenSvc --> LoginHandler: Access Token
        deactivate TokenSvc

        LoginHandler -> TokenSvc: GenerateRefreshToken(user)
        activate TokenSvc
        TokenSvc -> JWT: GenerateJwt(...)
        activate JWT
        JWT --> TokenSvc: Refresh Token
        deactivate JWT
        TokenSvc --> LoginHandler: Refresh Token
        deactivate TokenSvc

        LoginHandler --> Mediator: LoginPayload(\n  userAccountId, username,\n  refreshToken, accessToken)
        deactivate LoginHandler
        Mediator --> API: LoginPayload
        deactivate Mediator

        API -> User: 200 OK\n{\n  message: "Logged in successfully.",\n  payload: {\n    userAccountId, username,\n    refreshToken, accessToken\n  }\n}
      end
    end
  end
deactivate API

== Refresh Token Flow ==

User -> API: POST /api/auth/refresh\nHeader: X-Refresh-Token: <token>
activate API

API -> Mediator: Send(RefreshTokenCommand(refreshToken))
activate Mediator

note right of Mediator
  ValidationBehavior runs RefreshTokenValidator:
  refreshToken must be non-empty. Anonymous
  endpoint - no Bearer token required.
end note

alt Validation fails
  Mediator -> API: throws FluentValidation.ValidationException
  API -> User: 400 Bad Request\n{message: "Validation failed", errors: {...}}
else Validation succeeds

  Mediator -> RefreshHandler: Handle(command)
  activate RefreshHandler

  RefreshHandler -> TokenSvc: RefreshTokenAsync(refreshToken)
  activate TokenSvc

  TokenSvc -> JWT: ValidateRefreshTokenAsync(refreshToken)
  activate JWT
  note right of JWT
    Validates signature/expiry against the
    refresh token secret, extracts userId/
    username claims.
  end note
  JWT --> TokenSvc: ValidatedToken or throws
  deactivate JWT

  alt Token invalid or expired
    TokenSvc -> RefreshHandler: throw UnauthorizedException
    RefreshHandler -> Mediator: propagate
    Mediator -> API: propagate
    API -> User: 401 Unauthorized
  else Token valid

    TokenSvc -> UserMgr: FindByIdAsync(validated.UserId)
    activate UserMgr
    UserMgr -> UserStore: FindByIdAsync(userId)
    activate UserStore
    UserStore -> DB: SELECT UserAccountID, Username, ...\nFROM dbo.UserAccount\nWHERE UserAccountID = @Id
    activate DB
    DB --> UserStore: row or null
    deactivate DB
    UserStore --> UserMgr: ApplicationUser or null
    deactivate UserStore
    UserMgr --> TokenSvc: ApplicationUser or null
    deactivate UserMgr

    alt User not found
      TokenSvc -> RefreshHandler: throw UnauthorizedException\n"User account not found"
      RefreshHandler -> Mediator: propagate
      Mediator -> API: propagate
      API -> User: 401 Unauthorized
    else User found
      TokenSvc -> JWT: GenerateAccessToken(user)\nGenerateRefreshToken(user)
      JWT --> TokenSvc: new access + refresh tokens
      TokenSvc --> RefreshHandler: RefreshTokenResult
      deactivate TokenSvc

      RefreshHandler --> Mediator: LoginPayload(\n  userId, username,\n  refreshToken, accessToken)
      deactivate RefreshHandler
      Mediator --> API: LoginPayload
      deactivate Mediator

      API -> User: 200 OK\n{message: "Token refreshed successfully.",\npayload: {...}}
    end
  end
end
deactivate API

== Confirm User Flow ==

User -> API: POST /api/auth/confirm?token=<token>\n(requires Bearer access token)
activate API

API -> Mediator: Send(ConfirmUserCommand(token))
activate Mediator

Mediator -> ConfirmHandler: Handle(command)
activate ConfirmHandler

ConfirmHandler -> TokenSvc: ValidateConfirmationTokenAsync(token)
activate TokenSvc
TokenSvc -> JWT: Validate against confirmation\ntoken secret, extract userId
activate JWT
JWT --> TokenSvc: ValidatedToken or throws
deactivate JWT
TokenSvc --> ConfirmHandler: ValidatedToken
deactivate TokenSvc

alt Token invalid or expired
  ConfirmHandler -> Mediator: throw UnauthorizedException
  Mediator -> API: propagate
  API -> User: 401 Unauthorized
else Token valid

  ConfirmHandler -> UserMgr: FindByIdAsync(validatedToken.UserId)
  activate UserMgr
  UserMgr -> UserStore: FindByIdAsync(userId)
  activate UserStore
  UserStore -> DB: SELECT ...\nFROM dbo.UserAccount\nWHERE UserAccountID = @Id
  activate DB
  DB --> UserStore: row or null
  deactivate DB
  UserStore --> UserMgr: ApplicationUser or null
  deactivate UserStore
  UserMgr --> ConfirmHandler: ApplicationUser or null
  deactivate UserMgr

  alt User not found
    ConfirmHandler -> Mediator: throw UnauthorizedException\n"User account not found"
    Mediator -> API: propagate
    API -> User: 401 Unauthorized
  else User found

    ConfirmHandler -> UserStore: SetEmailConfirmedAsync(user, true)
    note right of UserStore
      IUserEmailStore<ApplicationUser> is injected
      directly into the handler (not via UserManager),
      setting the confirmed flag in-memory here.
    end note

    ConfirmHandler -> UserMgr: UpdateAsync(user)
    activate UserMgr
    UserMgr -> UserStore: UpdateAsync(user)
    activate UserStore
    UserStore -> DB: UPDATE dbo.UserAccount SET ...
    UserStore -> DB: INSERT INTO dbo.UserVerification\n(UserAccountId, VerificationDateTime)
    note right of UserStore
      Idempotent: skipped (duplicate-key
      exception swallowed) if a verification
      row already exists.
    end note
    UserStore --> UserMgr: IdentityResult.Success
    deactivate UserStore
    UserMgr --> ConfirmHandler: IdentityResult
    deactivate UserMgr

    ConfirmHandler --> Mediator: ConfirmationPayload(\n  user.Id, DateTime.UtcNow)
    deactivate ConfirmHandler
    Mediator --> API: ConfirmationPayload
    deactivate Mediator

    API -> User: 200 OK\n{message: "User with ID {id} is confirmed.",\npayload: {...}}
  end
end
deactivate API

== Resend Confirmation Email Flow ==

User -> API: POST /api/auth/confirm/resend?userId=<id>\n(requires Bearer access token)
activate API

API -> Mediator: Send(ResendConfirmationEmailCommand(userId))
activate Mediator

Mediator -> ResendHandler: Handle(command)
activate ResendHandler

ResendHandler -> UserMgr: FindByIdAsync(userId)
activate UserMgr
UserMgr -> UserStore: FindByIdAsync(userId)
activate UserStore
UserStore -> DB: SELECT ...\nFROM dbo.UserAccount\nWHERE UserAccountID = @Id
activate DB
DB --> UserStore: row or null
deactivate DB
UserStore --> UserMgr: ApplicationUser or null
deactivate UserStore
UserMgr --> ResendHandler: ApplicationUser or null
deactivate UserMgr

alt User not found
  ResendHandler -> ResendHandler: return silently\n(prevents user enumeration)
else User found

  ResendHandler -> UserMgr: IsEmailConfirmedAsync(user)
  UserMgr --> ResendHandler: bool

  alt Already confirmed
    ResendHandler -> ResendHandler: return silently (no-op)
  else Not yet confirmed

    ResendHandler -> TokenSvc: GenerateConfirmationToken(user)
    activate TokenSvc
    TokenSvc --> ResendHandler: confirmation token
    deactivate TokenSvc

    ResendHandler -> Mediator: Send(SendResendConfirmationEmailCommand)
    activate Mediator
    Mediator -> EmailDispatcher: SendResendConfirmationEmailAsync(\n  firstName, email, confirmationToken)
    activate EmailDispatcher
    EmailDispatcher -> Template: Render email\n(same Razor pipeline as registration)
    EmailDispatcher -> SMTP: SendAsync(email, subject, body)
    deactivate EmailDispatcher
    deactivate Mediator
  end
end

ResendHandler --> Mediator: (void)
deactivate ResendHandler
Mediator --> API: (void)
deactivate Mediator

API -> User: 200 OK\n{message: "confirmation email has been resent"}
note right of API
  Always 200 OK regardless of outcome above -
  same user-enumeration precaution as a not-found
  user or an already-confirmed account.
end note
deactivate API

== Update Username Flow ==

User -> API: PATCH /api/auth/username\n{newUsername}\n(requires Bearer access token)
activate API

API -> Mediator: Send(UpdateUsernameCommand(\n  GetAuthenticatedUserId(), newUsername))
activate Mediator

note right of Mediator
  ValidationBehavior runs UpdateUsernameValidator
  (same format rules as registration)
end note

alt Validation fails
  Mediator -> API: throws FluentValidation.ValidationException
  API -> User: 400 Bad Request
else Validation succeeds

  Mediator -> UpdateUsernameHandler: Handle(command)
  activate UpdateUsernameHandler

  UpdateUsernameHandler -> UserMgr: FindByIdAsync(userAccountId)
  activate UserMgr
  UserMgr -> UserStore: FindByIdAsync(userAccountId)
  activate UserStore
  UserStore -> DB: SELECT ...\nFROM dbo.UserAccount\nWHERE UserAccountID = @Id
  activate DB
  DB --> UserStore: row or null
  deactivate DB
  UserStore --> UserMgr: ApplicationUser or null
  deactivate UserStore
  UserMgr --> UpdateUsernameHandler: ApplicationUser or null
  deactivate UserMgr

  alt Account not found
    UpdateUsernameHandler -> Mediator: throw NotFoundException
    Mediator -> API: propagate
    API -> User: 404 Not Found
  else Account found

    UpdateUsernameHandler -> UserMgr: SetUserNameAsync(user, newUsername)
    activate UserMgr
    UserMgr -> UserStore: FindByNameAsync(newUsername)
    note right of UserMgr
      Uniqueness check before the UPDATE.
    end note
    UserMgr -> UserStore: UpdateAsync(user)
    UserStore -> DB: UPDATE dbo.UserAccount\nSET Username = @UserName, ...
    UserStore --> UserMgr: IdentityResult
    UserMgr --> UpdateUsernameHandler: IdentityResult
    deactivate UserMgr

    alt !result.Succeeded
      UpdateUsernameHandler -> Mediator: throw ConflictException\n(DuplicateUserName code ->\n"Username already exists")
      Mediator -> API: propagate
      API -> User: 409 Conflict
    else result.Succeeded
      UpdateUsernameHandler --> Mediator: UpdateUsernamePayload(\n  user.Id, user.UserName)
      deactivate UpdateUsernameHandler
      Mediator --> API: UpdateUsernamePayload
      deactivate Mediator
      API -> User: 200 OK\n{message: "Username updated successfully.",\npayload: {...}}
    end
  end
end
deactivate API

== Update Email Flow ==

User -> API: PATCH /api/auth/email\n{newEmail}\n(requires Bearer access token)
activate API

API -> Mediator: Send(UpdateEmailCommand(\n  GetAuthenticatedUserId(), newEmail))
activate Mediator

note right of Mediator
  ValidationBehavior runs UpdateEmailValidator
  (same format rules as registration)
end note

alt Validation fails
  Mediator -> API: throws FluentValidation.ValidationException
  API -> User: 400 Bad Request
else Validation succeeds

  Mediator -> UpdateEmailHandler: Handle(command)
  activate UpdateEmailHandler

  UpdateEmailHandler -> UserMgr: FindByIdAsync(userAccountId)
  activate UserMgr
  UserMgr -> UserStore: FindByIdAsync(userAccountId)
  UserStore -> DB: SELECT ...
  UserStore --> UserMgr: ApplicationUser or null
  UserMgr --> UpdateEmailHandler: ApplicationUser or null
  deactivate UserMgr

  alt Account not found
    UpdateEmailHandler -> Mediator: throw NotFoundException
    Mediator -> API: propagate
    API -> User: 404 Not Found
  else Account found

    UpdateEmailHandler -> UserMgr: SetEmailAsync(user, newEmail)
    activate UserMgr
    UserMgr -> UserStore: FindByEmailAsync(newEmail)
    note right of UserMgr
      Uniqueness check. Also resets
      user.EmailConfirmed = false -
      the caller must re-confirm via
      POST /api/auth/confirm/resend.
    end note
    UserMgr -> UserStore: UpdateAsync(user)
    UserStore -> DB: UPDATE dbo.UserAccount\nSET Email = @Email, ...
    UserStore -> DB: DELETE FROM dbo.UserVerification\nWHERE UserAccountID = @Id
    UserStore --> UserMgr: IdentityResult
    UserMgr --> UpdateEmailHandler: IdentityResult
    deactivate UserMgr

    alt !result.Succeeded
      UpdateEmailHandler -> Mediator: throw ConflictException\n(DuplicateEmail code ->\n"Email address already exists")
      Mediator -> API: propagate
      API -> User: 409 Conflict
    else result.Succeeded
      UpdateEmailHandler --> Mediator: UpdateEmailPayload(\n  user.Id, user.Email,\n  user.EmailConfirmed = false)
      deactivate UpdateEmailHandler
      Mediator --> API: UpdateEmailPayload
      deactivate Mediator
      API -> User: 200 OK\n{message: "Email updated successfully.",\npayload: {...}}
    end
  end
end
deactivate API

== Update Password Flow ==

User -> API: PATCH /api/auth/password\n{currentPassword, newPassword}\n(requires Bearer access token)
activate API

API -> Mediator: Send(UpdatePasswordCommand(\n  GetAuthenticatedUserId(),\n  currentPassword, newPassword))
activate Mediator

note right of Mediator
  ValidationBehavior runs UpdatePasswordValidator
  (same password strength rules as registration)
end note

alt Validation fails
  Mediator -> API: throws FluentValidation.ValidationException
  API -> User: 400 Bad Request
else Validation succeeds

  Mediator -> UpdatePasswordHandler: Handle(command)
  activate UpdatePasswordHandler

  UpdatePasswordHandler -> UserMgr: FindByIdAsync(userAccountId)
  activate UserMgr
  UserMgr -> UserStore: FindByIdAsync(userAccountId)
  UserStore --> UserMgr: ApplicationUser or null
  UserMgr --> UpdatePasswordHandler: ApplicationUser or null
  deactivate UserMgr

  alt Account not found
    UpdatePasswordHandler -> Mediator: throw NotFoundException
    Mediator -> API: propagate
    API -> User: 404 Not Found
  else Account found

    UpdatePasswordHandler -> UserMgr: ChangePasswordAsync(\n  user, currentPassword, newPassword)
    activate UserMgr
    UserMgr -> Argon2: VerifyHashedPassword(\n  user, user.PasswordHash, currentPassword)
    activate Argon2
    Argon2 --> UserMgr: Success/Failed
    deactivate Argon2

    alt Current password mismatch
      UserMgr --> UpdatePasswordHandler: IdentityResult.Failed\n(PasswordMismatch)
    else Current password matches
      UserMgr -> Argon2: HashPassword(user, newPassword)
      activate Argon2
      Argon2 --> UserMgr: new hash
      deactivate Argon2
      UserMgr -> UserStore: SetPasswordHashAsync(user, newHash)
      activate UserStore
      UserStore -> DB: UPDATE dbo.UserCredential\nSET IsRevoked = 1, RevokedAt = GETDATE()\nWHERE UserAccountId = @Id AND IsRevoked = 0
      UserStore -> DB: INSERT INTO dbo.UserCredential\n(UserAccountId, Hash)
      note right of UserStore
        Revoke-then-insert runs inside one
        DbTransaction (credential rotation).
      end note
      UserStore --> UserMgr: (void)
      deactivate UserStore
      UserMgr --> UpdatePasswordHandler: IdentityResult.Success
    end
    deactivate UserMgr

    alt Current password is incorrect
      UpdatePasswordHandler -> Mediator: throw UnauthorizedException\n"Current password is incorrect"
      Mediator -> API: propagate
      API -> User: 401 Unauthorized
    else !result.Succeeded (other failure)
      UpdatePasswordHandler -> Mediator: throw ConflictException
      Mediator -> API: propagate
      API -> User: 409 Conflict
    else result.Succeeded
      UpdatePasswordHandler --> Mediator: UpdatePasswordPayload(\n  user.Id, DateTime.UtcNow)
      deactivate UpdatePasswordHandler
      Mediator --> API: UpdatePasswordPayload
      deactivate Mediator
      API -> User: 200 OK\n{message: "Password updated successfully.",\npayload: {...}}
    end
  end
end
deactivate API

== Update Profile Flow ==

User -> API: PATCH /api/auth/profile\n{firstName, lastName, dateOfBirth}\n(requires Bearer access token)
activate API

API -> Mediator: Send(UpdateProfileCommand(\n  GetAuthenticatedUserId(),\n  firstName, lastName, dateOfBirth))
activate Mediator

note right of Mediator
  ValidationBehavior runs UpdateProfileValidator
  (same name/DateOfBirth rules as registration)
end note

alt Validation fails
  Mediator -> API: throws FluentValidation.ValidationException
  API -> User: 400 Bad Request
else Validation succeeds

  Mediator -> UpdateProfileHandler: Handle(command)
  activate UpdateProfileHandler

  UpdateProfileHandler -> UserMgr: FindByIdAsync(userAccountId)
  activate UserMgr
  UserMgr -> UserStore: FindByIdAsync(userAccountId)
  UserStore --> UserMgr: ApplicationUser or null
  UserMgr --> UpdateProfileHandler: ApplicationUser or null
  deactivate UserMgr

  alt Account not found
    UpdateProfileHandler -> Mediator: throw NotFoundException
    Mediator -> API: propagate
    API -> User: 404 Not Found
  else Account found

    UpdateProfileHandler -> UpdateProfileHandler: user.FirstName = ...\nuser.LastName = ...\nuser.DateOfBirth = ...
    note right of UpdateProfileHandler
      First/last name and date of birth aren't
      tracked by any Identity store interface -
      mutated directly on the ApplicationUser,
      then saved via UserManager.UpdateAsync.
    end note

    UpdateProfileHandler -> UserMgr: UpdateAsync(user)
    activate UserMgr
    UserMgr -> UserStore: UpdateAsync(user)
    UserStore -> DB: UPDATE dbo.UserAccount\nSET FirstName = @FirstName,\n    LastName = @LastName,\n    DateOfBirth = @DateOfBirth, ...
    UserStore --> UserMgr: IdentityResult
    UserMgr --> UpdateProfileHandler: IdentityResult
    deactivate UserMgr

    alt !result.Succeeded
      UpdateProfileHandler -> Mediator: throw ConflictException
      Mediator -> API: propagate
      API -> User: 409 Conflict
    else result.Succeeded
      UpdateProfileHandler --> Mediator: UpdateProfilePayload(\n  user.Id, firstName,\n  lastName, dateOfBirth)
      deactivate UpdateProfileHandler
      Mediator --> API: UpdateProfilePayload
      deactivate Mediator
      API -> User: 200 OK\n{message: "Profile updated successfully.",\npayload: {...}}
    end
  end
end
deactivate API

== Delete Account Flow ==

User -> API: DELETE /api/auth/account\n(requires Bearer access token)
activate API

API -> Mediator: Send(DeleteAccountCommand(\n  GetAuthenticatedUserId()))
activate Mediator

Mediator -> DeleteAccountHandler: Handle(command)
activate DeleteAccountHandler

DeleteAccountHandler -> UserMgr: FindByIdAsync(userAccountId)
activate UserMgr
UserMgr -> UserStore: FindByIdAsync(userAccountId)
UserStore --> UserMgr: ApplicationUser or null
UserMgr --> DeleteAccountHandler: ApplicationUser or null
deactivate UserMgr

alt Account not found
  DeleteAccountHandler -> Mediator: throw NotFoundException
  Mediator -> API: propagate
  API -> User: 404 Not Found
else Account found

  DeleteAccountHandler -> UserMgr: DeleteAsync(user)
  activate UserMgr
  UserMgr -> UserStore: DeleteAsync(user)
  activate UserStore
  UserStore -> DB: DELETE FROM dbo.UserAccount\nWHERE UserAccountID = @Id
  note right of UserStore
    UserCredential/UserVerification/UserAvatar
    cascade on delete. Posts, comments, photos,
    and follows use ON DELETE NO ACTION - if any
    reference this account, the DELETE throws a
    foreign key violation (SQL error 547).
  end note

  alt Foreign key violation (dependent records exist)
    UserStore --> UserMgr: IdentityResult.Failed\n(AccountHasDependentRecords)
  else Delete succeeds
    UserStore --> UserMgr: IdentityResult.Success
  end
  deactivate UserStore
  UserMgr --> DeleteAccountHandler: IdentityResult
  deactivate UserMgr

  alt Account has dependent records
    DeleteAccountHandler -> Mediator: throw ConflictException\n"Account cannot be deleted while it still\nhas associated posts, comments, photos,\nor follows."
    Mediator -> API: propagate
    API -> User: 409 Conflict
  else !result.Succeeded (other failure)
    DeleteAccountHandler -> Mediator: throw ConflictException
    Mediator -> API: propagate
    API -> User: 409 Conflict
  else result.Succeeded
    DeleteAccountHandler --> Mediator: (void)
    deactivate DeleteAccountHandler
    Mediator --> API: (void)
    deactivate Mediator
    API -> User: 200 OK\n{message: "Account deleted successfully."}
  end
end
deactivate API

== Error Handling (Global Exception Filter) ==

note over API
  API.Core's GlobalExceptionFilter catches:
  - FluentValidation.ValidationException -> 400 Bad Request\n    {message, errors} (grouped by property)
  - ConflictException -> 409 Conflict
  - NotFoundException -> 404 Not Found
  - UnauthorizedException -> 401 Unauthorized
  - ForbiddenException -> 403 Forbidden
  - Domain.Exceptions.ValidationException -> 400 Bad Request
  - Microsoft.Data.SqlClient.SqlException -> 503 Service Unavailable
  - All others -> 500 Internal Server Error
end note

@enduml
